# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line 1 (above the blank line) is your commit subject — imperative, ~50 chars.
#
# UX Conformance block (persists in the message — the lines WITHOUT a #):
#   • One mark per principle: ✅ or N/A.  P5: if you added syntax, say what it RETIRES.
#   • "New non-conformances": file each gap as UXP-NN in guidance/ux-remediation.md, or "none".
#   • If this commit has NO UI surface, replace the whole block with:  UI: none
#
# HYGIENE: no agent attribution, no session links. Never end a message with a
#   Co-Authored-By: Claude... / Claude-Session: ... / "Generated with" line.
#   A HUMAN Co-Authored-By is fine. CI (commit-hygiene) rejects the rest.
#
# Full process: guidance/ux-definition-of-done.md → "How this gate is run".
# Rule: no Conformance Statement, no merge.
#
# Enable this template once (repo-local) - it does NOTHING until you run this:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
# (place this file at the repo root as .gitmessage)
